msgid "Setting up SITL on Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:7
#: daa203ed0ebb4ec39dac598dd28a05ee
msgid "This page describes how to setup the :ref:`SITL (Software In The Loop) <sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop>` on Linux. The specific commands were tested on Ubuntu from 12.10 to 18.04."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:11
#: f7142ab8adb44cabbe67639df85fd5fd
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:13
#: a709433839ff4fbb88c97d27929484c3
msgid "The SITL simulator allows you to run Plane, Copter or Rover without any hardware. It is a build of the autopilot code using an ordinary C++ compiler, giving you a native executable that allows you to test the behaviour of the code without hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:18
#: 41149db409ca465ab37a94b659e6a955
msgid "SITL runs natively on Linux and Windows. See the separate :ref:`windows installation page <sitl-native-on-windows>` for a windows install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:25
#: 2c02d52d07c047dca7e44a429ce603bb
msgid "Install steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:27
#: 8079ab80d4c347138e973ead02f5981f
msgid "Please follow the instructions in :ref:`Setting up the Build Environment (Linux/Ubuntu) <building-setup-linux>` to set up the full environment, including SITL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:30
#: 376ea0b1e7a44a308055fe8f54993bb1
msgid "Start SITL simulator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:32
#: 9a6f4682598e4dbfba53cdc87f00af16
msgid "To start the simulator first change directory to the vehicle directory. For examples below, for the Multicopter code change to **ardupilot/ArduCopter**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:41
#: 65b2708a8d9f47a795a12a1e3895550f
msgid "Then start the simulator using **sim_vehicle.py**. The first time you run it, you should use the ``-w`` option to wipe the virtual EEPROM of user changed parameters and load the default parameters for your vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:49
#: 7cd1ed1cb6d94baf81a7ab6ed1efd93f
msgid "Alternatively, if not starting in the ArduCopter directory, but at the base **ardupilot** directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:58
#: c4703137adf644619f8f95398e6ffca7
msgid "`sim_vehicle.py <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/autotest/sim_vehicle.py>`__ has many useful options, ranging from setting the simulation speed through to choosing the initial vehicle location. These can be listed by calling it with the ``-h`` flag (and some are demonstrated in :ref:`Using SITL for ArduPilot Testing <using-sitl-for-ardupilot-testing>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:65
#: 17579000ed89425eb2a3bcabbae5951b
msgid "If the map tiles don't load, you can temporarily change the map provider in the map window by clicking View/Service. To keep the new map service between launches, add the following lines to the end of your \".bashrc\" (change MicrosoftHyb to the provider you want):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:74
#: cec8840832114f28b104e4813d161c68
msgid "Learn MAVProxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:76
#: c11b1f2373ac4b84bfe96e934b926b4d
msgid "To get the most out of SITL you really need to learn to use MAVProxy. Have a read of the :ref:`MAVProxy documentation <mavproxy:home>`. Enjoy flying!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:80
#: 4f8778205c854dbdb283744c3b51d6e3
msgid "Updating MAVProxy and pymavlink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/setting-up-sitl-on-linux.rst:82
#: 4b290d82a5ff4991a52a485aa4340548
